{
 "id": "puc1-electronics-06-rectifiers-and-filters.t4.lesson",
 "chapterId": "puc1-electronics-06-rectifiers-and-filters",
 "topicId": "puc1-electronics-06-rectifiers-and-filters.t4",
 "title": {
  "en": "Filters: capacitor, inductor, LC and π filters",
  "kn": "ಸೋಸುಕಗಳು (ಫಿಲ್ಟರ್‌ಗಳು): ಧಾರಕ, ಪ್ರೇರಕ, LC ಮತ್ತು π"
 },
 "minutes": 40,
 "blocks": [
  {
   "id": "intro",
   "type": "intro",
   "heading": {
    "en": "Smoothing the bumps",
    "kn": "ಉಬ್ಬುಗಳನ್ನು ನಯಗೊಳಿಸುವುದು"
   },
   "hook": {
    "en": "Connect a speaker to a bare rectifier and you hear a loud hum: that is the ripple. A filter removes most of it before the d.c. reaches the circuit.",
    "kn": "ಕೇವಲ ದಿಷ್ಟಕಾರಿಗೆ ಸ್ಪೀಕರ್ ಸೇರಿಸಿದರೆ ಜೋರಾದ ಗುನುಗು ಕೇಳುತ್ತದೆ: ಅದೇ ತರಂಗಾಂಶ (ರಿಪಲ್). ಫಿಲ್ಟರ್ ಅದರ ಹೆಚ್ಚಿನ ಭಾಗವನ್ನು ತೆಗೆದುಹಾಕುತ್ತದೆ."
   },
   "objectives": [
    {
     "en": "Explain the action of a shunt capacitor filter"
    },
    {
     "en": "Explain series inductor, LC and π filters"
    },
    {
     "en": "Calculate the ripple factor of a capacitor filter"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "Connect a speaker to a bare rectifier and you hear a loud hum: that is the ripple. A filter removes most of it before the d.c. reaches the circuit.",
    "kn": "ಕೇವಲ ದಿಷ್ಟಕಾರಿಗೆ ಸ್ಪೀಕರ್ ಸೇರಿಸಿದರೆ ಜೋರಾದ ಗುನುಗು ಕೇಳುತ್ತದೆ: ಅದೇ ತರಂಗಾಂಶ (ರಿಪಲ್). ಫಿಲ್ಟರ್ ಅದರ ಹೆಚ್ಚಿನ ಭಾಗವನ್ನು ತೆಗೆದುಹಾಕುತ್ತದೆ."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "concept1",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Shunt capacitor filter"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "A capacitor connected across the load charges to the peak V_m during each pulse. When the rectifier output falls, the diode turns off and the capacitor discharges slowly through R_L until the next pulse recharges it. The output becomes nearly steady d.c. with a small saw-tooth ripple. The larger the time constant C R_L compared with the time between pulses, the smaller the ripple: $r = 1/(4\\sqrt{3} f C R_L)$ for full-wave and $1/(2\\sqrt{3} f C R_L)$ for half-wave."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "C across R_L; charges to V_m"
    },
    {
     "en": "Discharges slowly between peaks"
    },
    {
     "en": "Ripple ↓ when C, R_L or f ↑"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "The shunt capacitor charges to the peak and discharges slowly through the load between pulses. A larger capacitor or a lighter load gives less ripple.",
    "kn": "ಸಮಾಂತರ ಧಾರಕ ಶಿಖರ ವೋಲ್ಟೇಜ್‌ಗೆ ಆವೇಶಗೊಂಡು ಪಲ್ಸ್‌ಗಳ ನಡುವೆ ಲೋಡ್ ಮೂಲಕ ನಿಧಾನವಾಗಿ ವಿಸರ್ಜಿಸುತ್ತದೆ. ದೊಡ್ಡ ಧಾರಕ ಅಥವಾ ಹಗುರ ಲೋಡ್ ಕಡಿಮೆ ತರಂಗಾಂಶ ನೀಡುತ್ತದೆ."
   },
   "formula": "r_{FW} = \\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{3}\\,f C R_L},\\qquad r_{HW} = \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{3}\\,f C R_L}"
  },
