  {
   "id": "concept2",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Inductor, LC and π filters"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "A choke (inductor) in series with the load opposes changes in current: its reactance ωL is high for the ripple and nearly zero for d.c. For full-wave, $r = R_L/(3\\sqrt{2}\\,\\omega L)$, so it works best with heavy loads (small R_L). The LC (choke-input) filter combines a series L with a shunt C and gives low ripple with good regulation. The π filter (C–L–C) gives a higher d.c. output and very low ripple, but poorer regulation."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "Choke: series L, better for heavy loads"
    },
    {
     "en": "LC: series L + shunt C"
    },
    {
     "en": "π filter: C–L–C, very low ripple"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "A choke in series blocks the ripple and passes d.c. An LC filter combines both elements, and the pi filter, C L C, gives the smoothest output.",
    "kn": "ಸರಣಿಯ ಚೋಕ್ ತರಂಗಾಂಶವನ್ನು ತಡೆದು ನೇರ ಪ್ರವಾಹ ಹಾಯಿಸುತ್ತದೆ. LC ಫಿಲ್ಟರ್ ಎರಡನ್ನೂ ಸೇರಿಸುತ್ತದೆ; π ಫಿಲ್ಟರ್ (C-L-C) ಅತಿ ನಯವಾದ ಔಟ್‌ಪುಟ್ ನೀಡುತ್ತದೆ."
   }
